{% extends 'pages/_base.jinja' %}


{% block content %}

  <section class="recipe-details">
    <h2>Blueberry muffin recipe</h2>

     <img src="/static/images/blueberry_muffin.jpg" alt="Raspberry and white chocolate">
    
    <p>This is a raspberry and white chocolate muffin</p>
     <ul>
       <li>Preperation time: 10min</li>
       <li>Cook time: 20min</li>
       <li>Total time: 30min</li>
     </ul>

    <h3>Ingredients</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>1 ½ cups (195 g) all-purpose flour </li>
      <li>¾ cup (150 g) granulated sugar, plus 1 tablespoon for muffin tops</li>
      <li>2 teaspoons aluminum-free baking powder</li>
      <li>¼ teaspoon fine sea salt</li>
      <li>⅓ cup (80 ml) vegetable oil, safflower oil, or avocado oil</li>
      <li>1 large egg</li>
      <li>⅓ cup (80 ml) milk or non-dairy milk, plus more as needed</li>
      <li>1 ½ teaspoons vanilla extract</li>
      <li>6 to 8 ounces fresh or frozen blueberries (heaped 1 cup)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Instructions</h3>

    <ol>
      <li>Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C).</li>
      <li>In a large bowl, whisk the flour, sugar, baking powder, and salt until well blended.</li>
      <li>Choose a measuring jug that holds at least 1 cup. Add the oil to the jug, and then crack in the egg. Pour in enough milk to reach the 1-cup line on the jug (about ⅓ cup of milk). Add the vanilla extract and whisk until everything is combined.</li>
      <li>Pour the wet ingredients into the bowl with the dry ingredients. Use a spoon or rubber spatula to stir gently until the batter comes together. Fold in the blueberries. Be careful not to overmix! The batter will be thick (see tips below).</li>
      <li>Divide the batter between muffin cups. If making big-topped muffins, the batter will come to the tops of the paper liners. Sprinkle a little sugar on top of each muffin.</li>
      <li>Bake muffins for 15 to 20 minutes or until the tops are no longer wet and a toothpick inserted into the middle of a muffin comes out with crumbs, not wet batter. Transfer to a cooling rack.</li>
      
    

    </ol>
  </section>


{% endblock %}

